---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CvHeader from '../components/cv/CvHeader.astro';
import CvSection from '../components/cv/CvSection.astro';
import CvItem from '../components/cv/CvItem.astro';
import CvTagList from '../components/cv/CvTagList.astro';
import CvList from '../components/cv/CvList.astro';
import CvListItem from '../components/cv/CvListItem.astro';
import CvSkillsGrid from '../components/cv/CvSkillsGrid.astro';
import CvSkillsCategory from '../components/cv/CvSkillsCategory.astro';

const title = 'CV - Aleksandra';
const description = 'My personal CV.';
const permalink = `${Astro.site?.href}cv`;
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} permalink={permalink} current="cv">
  <div class="container">
    <CvHeader
      title="Aleksandra Glesaaen Ødegård"
      tagline="Advocate of good academic software"
    />

    <!-- Contact information -->
    <CvSection title="📧 Contact">
      <CvList>
        <CvListItem
          key="Email"
          icon="mdi:email"
          icon_size="1.2em"
          value="aleksandra@glesaaen.com"
          value_ref="mailto:aleksandra@glesaaen.com" />
        <CvListItem
          key="GitHub"
          icon="mdi:github"
          icon_size="1.3em"
          value="Irubataru"
          value_ref="https://github.com/Irubataru" />
        <CvListItem
          key="LinkedIn"
          icon="mdi:linkedin"
          icon_size="1.3em"
          value="Aleksandra Glesaaen Ødegård"
          value_ref="https://www.linkedin.com/in/aleksandra-glesaaen-ødegård-49a367158" />
        </CvList>
    </CvSection>

    <!-- Work experience -->
    <CvSection title="💼 Work Experience">
      <CvItem date="2024-11 - Present">
        <Fragment slot="title">
          <h3>Omegapoint Norge</h3>
          <h4>Expert</h4>
        </Fragment>
        <p>
          At Omegapoint I led multiple internal projects focused on technology
          exploration and process optimization, expanding my expertise in
          frontend development, Azure cloud services, and Kubernetes
          orchestration. I developed an AI-driven search solution for the
          company event system and drove significant process improvements by
          standardizing integration testing practices to align with industry
          standards and restructuring project architectures to follow
          established conventions.
        </p>
        <Fragment slot="tags">
          <CvTagList
            tags={[
              "C# .NET",
              "Python",
              "Next.js",
              "Azure",
              "AI",
              "Docker",
              "Kubernetes",
              "CI/CD",
              "Integration testing",
              "Unit testing",
            ]}
            />
        </Fragment>
      </CvItem>

      <CvItem date="2021-05 - 2024-10">
        <Fragment slot="title">
          <h3>SINTEF Digital, Optimization</h3>
          <h4>Researcher</h4>
        </Fragment>
        <p>
          As a researcher in the optimization group at SINTEF, I have developed
          advanced algorithms and applications to address complex challenges in
          healthcare, the aviation industry, construction, quantum computing,
          and the architecture sector. In addition to my technical development
          work, I held market responsibility for the healthcare sector, where I
          worked closely with stakeholders to understand their specific needs
          and challenges, tailoring technological solutions that drive
          efficiency and innovation within the sector.
        </p>
        <Fragment slot="tags">
          <CvTagList
            tags={[
              "C# .NET",
              "Python",
              "Healthcare",
              "Optimization",
              "Quantum computing",
              "Research and development",
              "Project management",
              "APIs"
            ]}
          />
        </Fragment>
      </CvItem>

      <CvItem date="2018-10 - 2021-05">
        <Fragment slot="title">
          <h3>Share Control AS</h3>
          <h4>Software Developer and Project Leader</h4>
        </Fragment>
        <p>
          In my role as a software developer and project manager at
          ShareControl, I developed a customized application in Excel VBA to
          manage and monitor lease contracts in compliance with the IFRS 16
          accounting standard. The application was designed to provide clients
          with a straightforward overview and perform the necessary
          calculations as part of their accounting processes, while also being
          transparent and easily auditable to meet documentation and
          traceability requirements. Through this work, I gained significant
          experience in interdisciplinary collaboration and communication
          across fields.
        </p>
        <Fragment slot="tags">
          <CvTagList
            tags={[
              "VBA",
              "Python",
              "Project management",
              "IFRS 16",
              "Excel"
            ]}
          />
        </Fragment>
      </CvItem>

      <CvItem date="2016-10 - 2018-10">
        <Fragment slot="title">
          <h3>Department of Physics, Swansea University</h3>
          <h4>Postdoctoral Researcher</h4>
        </Fragment>
        <p>
          As a postdoctoral researcher at the Department of Physics at Swansea
          University, I worked on improving the performance and functionality
          of an existing C-based legacy code for advanced particle physics
          calculations. Through optimization and detailed adjustments,
          including the use of hand-written assembly operations, I achieved an
          impressive performance increase, with a 20x improvement compared to
          the previous code.
        </p>
        <p>
          She also gained valuable experience with unit
          testing of complex, parallelized code, contributing to increased
          reliability and maintainability. Additionally, Aleksandra explored
          applications of machine learning to open new research opportunities
          in hadron spectroscopy.
        </p>
        <Fragment slot="tags">
          <CvTagList
            tags={[
              "C",
              "C++",
              "Python",
              "Assembly",
              "Machine learning",
              "Physics"
            ]}
          />
        </Fragment>
      </CvItem>
    </CvSection>

    <!-- Education -->
    <CvSection title="🎓 Education">
      <CvItem date="2013 - 2016">
        <Fragment slot="title">
          <h3>Johann Wolfgang Goethe-Universitët</h3>
          <h4>PhD in Theoretical Physics</h4>
        </Fragment>
        <p>
          As a Ph.D. student in physics, I focused on developing effective
          theories to explore inaccessible regions of the quantum
          chromodynamics (QCD) phase diagram, particularly for cold and
          dense states. I developed advanced mathematical frameworks and
          applied graph-theoretical methods to solve complex equations
          analytically.
        </p>
        <p>
          Through my doctoral work, I gained solid expertise in research
          methodology and the use of high-performance computing (HPC) to
          manage extensive calculations. I participated in several
          international conferences, where I both presented and published
          my research findings.
        </p>
      </CvItem>

      <CvItem date="2008 - 2013">
        <Fragment slot="title">
          <h3>Norwegian University of Science and Technology (NTNU)</h3>
          <h4>Masters in Physics - Graduate of Excellence</h4>
        </Fragment>
        <p>
          As a master’s student in physics, I worked with effective models
          in high-energy particle physics to study the phase diagram of
          quantum chromodynamics (QCD). I compared various mathematical
          methods to solve complex equations and achieved valuable results.
          For my outstanding efforts, I was awarded the prize for best
          master’s student at the Faculty of Science.
        </p>
      </CvItem>
    </CvSection>

    <!-- Projects -->
    <CvSection title="🚀 Projects">
    </CvSection>

    <!-- Other experience -->
    <CvSection title="🌟 Other experience">
    </CvSection>

    <!-- Courses & certifications -->
    <CvSection title="🏆 Courses & Certifications">
    </CvSection>

    <!-- Languages -->
    <CvSection title="🌍 Languages">
      <CvList>
        <CvListItem
          key="Norwegian"
          emoji="🇳🇴"
          value="Native" />
        <CvListItem
          key="English"
          emoji="🇬🇧"
          value="Excellent" />
        <CvListItem
          key="Japanese"
          emoji="🇯🇵"
          value="Basic" />
        </CvList>
    </CvSection>

    <!-- Theses -->
    <CvSection title="📖 Theses">
      <CvItem date="2016.07.31" link="https://github.com/Irubataru/phd-thesis">
        <Fragment slot="title">
          <h3>Heavy Quark QCD at Finite Temperature and Density Using an Effective Theory</h3>
          <h4>PhD thesis</h4>
          <h5>Supervisors: Prof. Dr. Owe Philipsen, and Prof. Dr. Dirk-Hermann Rischke</h5>
        </Fragment>

        <p>
          In this work I used an effective theory approach to study the cold
          and dense limit of heavy QCD from first principles. I developed both
          computational and graphical tools and methods for carrying out the
          necessary mathematics to high order. Much of the work is also
          dedicated to the methods of resummation and their advantages.
        </p>
      </CvItem>

      <CvItem date="2013.05.31" link="https://ntnuopen.ntnu.no/ntnu-xmlui/handle/11250/246896">
        <Fragment slot="title">
          <h3>The Chiral Phase Transition in QCD: Mean-Field Versus the Functional Renormalisation Group</h3>
          <h4>Master thesis</h4>
          <h5>Supervisor: Prof. Jens Oluf Andersen</h5>
        </Fragment>

        <p>
          For my masters work I made use of low energy effective theories, more
          specifically the quark extended linear sigma model, to analyse the
          properties of the breaking of chiral symmetry in QCD, and the
          emerging phase diagram. Also made use of the functional
          renormalisation group to extract the correct low energy properties of
          the quantum field theory.
        </p>

      </CvItem>
    </CvSection>

    <!-- Publications -->
    <CvSection title="📚 Publications">
    </CvSection>

    <!-- Skills -->
    <CvSection title="🛠️ Skills">
      <CvSkillsGrid>
        <CvSkillsCategory
          title="Programming languages"
          skills={["C# .NET", "C", "C++", "Python", "TypeScript", "Rust", "Lua", "VBA"]}/>
        <CvSkillsCategory
          title="Technologies"
          skills={["Azure", "Docker", "Kubernetes", "Machine learning", "Optimization"]}/>
        <CvSkillsCategory
          title="Typography and frontend"
          skills={["Latex", "HTML", "CSS","Vue.js", "Astro", "React", "Next.js"]}/>
      </CvSkillsGrid>
    </CvSection>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
